{
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "1e1993ee-fd2d-4945-8a6c-d6d548395653",
      "name": "Current (v2)",
      "description": {
        "content": "Modern endpoints (recommended). Faster grid-index lookups, blended multi-model forecasts, explicit downscaling control, and a compact, date-keyed response shape. All paths start with `/v2/`.\n",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "97ab1821-02a7-4016-9981-9dc0325afea1",
          "name": "Historical weather (optimized grid lookup)",
          "request": {
            "name": "Historical weather (optimized grid lookup)",
            "description": {
              "content": "Historical weather for a coordinate pair using B-tree indexes on\npre-computed grid indices (`lat_idx`, `lon_idx`) instead of PostGIS\ngeography-based GIST indexes — significantly faster lookups.\n\nProvides 30+ years of ERA5 coverage (auto-fetched on first request),\nautomatic recent-history gap-filling, variable-aware temporal\naggregation, and optional ~1 km downscaling.\n\nGranularity controls how the daily values are aggregated:\n\n- `daily` → dates like `2025-01-15` (every day through the inclusive `end_date`)\n- `weekly` → ISO weeks like `2025-W03` (Mon–Sun, complete weeks only)\n- `monthly` → months like `2025-01` (complete calendar months only)\n\nCoordinates are snapped to the 0.25° grid. When both `start_date` and\n`end_date` are omitted, returns roughly the last 3 months.\n",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "history"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "lat",
                  "value": "<double>",
                  "description": "(Required) Latitude coordinate in decimal degrees."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "lon",
                  "value": "<double>",
                  "description": "(Required) Longitude coordinate in decimal degrees."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "var",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Weather variable(s). Supports comma-separated values (`var=temp_mean,precipitation`) or repeated parameters (`var=temp_mean&var=precipitation`). If omitted, all available variables are returned. See the Datasets section for units and availability.\n"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "var",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Weather variable(s). Supports comma-separated values (`var=temp_mean,precipitation`) or repeated parameters (`var=temp_mean&var=precipitation`). If omitted, all available variables are returned. See the Datasets section for units and availability.\n"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "start_date",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "Start date (inclusive) in `YYYY-MM-DD` format."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "end_date",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "End date (inclusive) in `YYYY-MM-DD` format."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "granularity",
                  "value": "daily",
                  "description": "Temporal granularity of the returned data."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "use_downscaling",
                  "value": "true",
                  "description": "Apply ~1 km downscaling when available."
                }
              ],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": null
          },
